<Base title="About Zak Plumridge — Data science & software" description="Meet Zak Plumridge: MSc Data Science graduate with experience delivering Python, React, PostgreSQL and API-driven applications."><div class="shell about-page"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT ME</p><h1>Curiosity, with a practical side<span class="blue">.</span></h1><p class="lead">I’m Zak Plumridge, based in Brighton. I build software and work with data to help people understand information and put it to use.</p><div class="about-links"><a class="button primary" href="/downloads/zak-plumridge-cv.pdf" download>Download CV (PDF)</a><a class="button secondary" href="mailto:zakplumridge@outlook.com">Email me</a><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/zakplumridge" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn →</a><a href="https://github.com/zakplum" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub →</a></div><section><h2>Experience that connects people, data and software.</h2><p>My experience spans application development, data research, operations and customer-facing roles. I enjoy understanding how people work, finding where information or processes get in their way, and building something that helps.</p><p>I’ve taken applications from requirements and data workflows through development, deployment, maintenance and staff training. Examples include Indy, a community intelligence platform built around approximately 14,000 supporter records, and Radar, which automated research across approximately 2,500 planning applications and transferred qualified leads to HubSpot.</p><p>Alongside this, my academic work has explored machine learning for harmful-language detection and the localisation of dark-matter halos from simulated astronomical observations. These projects developed my experience in preparing data, comparing models and evaluating what their predictions can tell us.</p><p>Previously, I’ve managed an engagement team of up to 12, monitored campaign performance and trained staff. Customer accounts and energy-services roles in the UK and New Zealand also shaped how I communicate, solve problems and work with different people.</p></section><section><h2>Technical skills.</h2><dl class="skills-list"><div><dt>Data & research</dt><dd>Python, SQL, NumPy, SciPy, scikit-learn, PyTorch, data cleaning, statistical analysis and model evaluation.</dd></div><div><dt>Software & delivery</dt><dd>React.js, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, REST APIs, Git, GitHub, Vercel and Railway.</dd></div><div><dt>Working with people</dt><dd>Requirements gathering, workflow design, stakeholder communication, user training and operational delivery.</dd></div></dl></section><section><h2>Qualifications.</h2><h3>MSc Data Science · University of Sussex</h3><p>Distinction · 2025–2026. My dissertation investigated halo localisation from simulated 21 cm maps, using U-Net models and evaluating their predictions and uncertainty. Dissertation mark: 84%.</p><h3>BSc Computer Science · Goldsmiths, University of London</h3><p>First Class Honours · 2021–2024. My final-year project, Fair Play, explored automated detection of harmful football comments to support faster moderation.</p></section><section id="contact"><h2>Let’s talk.</h2><p>I’m interested in opportunities across data science, analytics and software development. For roles, project questions or a conversation about my work, email <a class="inline-link" href="mailto:zakplumridge@outlook.com">zakplumridge@outlook.com</a>.</p></section></div></Base>
